---
// Warehouses and industrial sites — one of the THIRTEEN "by type of premises"
// leaf pages under the /commercial-cleaning/ hub (navigation.ts, "By type of
// premises" group). Built in one pass with its twelve siblings.
//
// NO CONTENT BRIEF EXISTS for any of the thirteen. All copy below is DRAFTED,
// not supplied. See src/pages/commercial-cleaning/office-cleaning.astro's header for the launch
// blockers shared across the whole cluster.
//
// ⚠️ THIS PAGE HAS TWO READERS WITH OPPOSITE BUDGETS, and getting the order
// right is the whole editorial decision. A warehouse manager searching
// "warehouse cleaning" usually wants the FLOOR — a scrubber down the aisles,
// dust off the racking, the dock swept. What they get quoted, and what they
// actually get complaints about, is the AMENITIES: the crib room, the
// bathrooms, the office. On an industrial site the amenities are the whole
// staff experience and they are the first line cut from a scope.
//
// So the page leads with the floor (which is what the search wanted) and
// spends its persuasion on the amenities (which is what the reader needs).
// §6 is that argument and it is deliberately the longest block on the page.
//
// WHAT MAKES THIS PAGE DIFFERENT structurally:
//   - `Callout tone="warning"` on the boundary FIRST, before any scope. On an
//     industrial site the dangerous thing is a cleaner who says yes to
//     everything: heights, plant, racking, spills of unknown substance. Same
//     pattern as the construction, medical and kitchen pages.
//   - `ServiceBlocks variant="icon-grid"` grouped by ZONE, then a second
//     `ContentGrid` that argues for the smallest zone. The asymmetry is the
//     point — see above.
//   - `ImageBand` twice is avoided; the dock frame goes in the ContentGrid as
//     an image cell instead, which is the only page in the cluster to use
//     `ContentGrid`'s `image` cell type.
//   - No `ComparisonTable`. Same call as strata, construction, medical,
//     schools and gyms: the shared rows are written for someone choosing who
//     enters their home.
//
// BLOCKS LAUNCH, specific to this page:
//   - EQUIPMENT. A warehouse floor needs a ride-on or walk-behind
//     autoscrubber. A mop on 2,000 square metres of concrete is not a
//     service. Bracketed in §4 and it decides whether this page is honest.
//   - Whether TLB will work at height at all. Bracketed in §3. High-level
//     racking dusting and high-bay light cleaning both need an EWP and a
//     licence, and the answer is probably no.
//   - Whether TLB will touch a spill of unknown substance. The answer must
//     be no. Stated as no in §3; confirm nobody softens it.
//   - Site induction and PPE requirements: whether TLB's team can meet a
//     typical industrial site induction. Bracketed in branded FAQ 1.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/sections/SiteHeader.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/sections/Hero.astro';
import TrustBar from '../../components/sections/TrustBar.astro';
import Backdrop from '../../components/ui/Backdrop.astro';
import TextBlock from '../../components/sections/TextBlock.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/sections/Callout.astro';
import ServiceBlocks from '../../components/sections/ServiceBlocks.astro';
import ContentGrid from '../../components/sections/ContentGrid.astro';
import TagCloud from '../../components/sections/TagCloud.astro';
import GoogleReviewSlider from '../../components/sections/GoogleReviewSlider.astro';
import { googleBusinessProfileUrl, googleReviews } from '../../data/googleReviews';
import Faq from '../../components/sections/Faq.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/sections/CallToAction.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/sections/SiteFooter.astro';
import logoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-horizontal.png';
// This page's own frames are in src/assets/commercial_cleaning/premises/;
// the prompts are in that folder's IMAGE-PROMPTS.md.
//
// ⚠️ THE HI-VIS EXCEPTION applies here, same as on the construction page.
// IMAGE-GUIDELINES §3 sets the canonical uniform as aqua polo, dark teal
// apron and teal gloves, and the palette rule forbids yellow. On a warehouse
// or industrial floor a cleaner wears a high-visibility vest, and
// fluorescent lime-green is the standard Australian hi-vis colour and the
// closest real one to the brand's Mint Green. A frame of a cleaner in an
// apron in a forklift aisle would be a photo of something that must not
// happen. The amenities frames keep the apron, because a crib room is not a
// traffic zone — which is itself the §6 argument in miniature.
// §2 backdrop, behind the Cream scrim — the homepage's, same as the hub.
import footerLogoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-square.png';
import {
  primaryNav,
  headerNav,
  headerSecondaryCta,
  footerServiceLinks,
  footerContact,
  footerCopyright,
  quoteCta,
} from '../../data/navigation';
// Brief §18. Southern Gold Coast was dropped from this page's town band and
// the subheading trimmed to match. Confirmed with the client as a BUILD
// REGRESSION rather than a deliberate footprint decision, so the three-region
// band is restored: BFD 2.1 requires the whole footprint named and the
// do-not-touch rules treat a trimmed list as a regression rather than a
// choice. Same band the commercial carpet and commercial pressure pages
// already render.
//
// This matters commercially HERE more than anywhere: the industrial estates at
// Tweed Heads South, Chinderah and across the border are exactly the sites
// this page is written for, and dropping the Gold Coast group removed the half
// of that corridor sitting in Queensland.
import { locationGroups, locationSubheading } from '../../data/locations';
import { trustBarCards } from '../../data/trust';
import { commercialBusiness, relatedPremises, walkthroughCtaLabel } from '../../data/premises';
import { howItWorks, managedForYou, theLineBody } from '../../data/brand-lines';
import { z } from 'astro/zod';
import { getPage } from '../../lib/cms';
import * as section from '../../lib/cms-schemas';
import { sized } from '../../lib/cms-schemas';

// §0 Metadata. Title and description are the SIGNED-OFF workbook text
// (Keyword Mapping & Metadata, sheet 1 row 37), reproduced verbatim. The old
// title carried neither "commercial" nor "services", so the mapped primary
// `commercial warehouse cleaning services` (60/mo) was absent; the old
// description ran 24 characters over, so the crib room and amenities clause —
// the page's whole argument — was the part being truncated.
//
// The approved meta is better than the old one on substance as well as
// length: leading with amenities rather than aisles matches the section this
// page spends most of its effort on, and it carries `commercial and
// industrial cleaning services` (50/mo) in substance through "industrial".
//
// ⚠️ CHANGE REQUEST FOR THE WORKBOOK OWNER, not blocking. The approved title
// drops "industrial" entirely, which is half of what this page sells, and the
// mapped secondary at 50/mo is 45% of this row's demand. The old title got the
// scope right and the keyword wrong; the approved one does the reverse.
// Suggested replacement, 56 characters:
//   'Commercial Warehouse & Industrial Cleaning | TLB Cleaning'
// Until that is decided, the eyebrow label in §1 is the only thing above the
// fold still naming half the service, which is why it is left alone.
//
// In `pageMeta`, on `canonical`:
// ⚠️ Placeholder domain, same as every sibling page. Confirm before launch.

// Brief §7. The approved workbook CTA is the full sentence `Talk to us about
// your site today`, which at 32 characters is long for a button: per Rule 4
// the sentence goes in the closing block's lead-in and the button takes its
// imperative core at 26. Both come from the same approved text. One primary
// CTA, repeated, per BFD 9.5.
//
// ⚠️ WORTH THE SAME REVIEW as the kitchen and hospitality CTAs, not blocking.
// The label this replaces, `Book a site walkthrough` (walkthroughCtaLabel in
// data/premises.ts, still used by the sibling premises pages), is the more
// specific ask, and this page makes the walkthrough case explicitly by listing
// the four things it looks at. `Talk to us about your site` is softer. It is
// placeable and it is placed.
//
// No BFD 13.2 conflict on this page: there is no `Get an instant quote` on it
// and the pricing block promises a walkthrough and a written scope.

// §1 Hero. `split-single-image`, image right, matching the rest of the
// commercial cluster. `imageFocus="86%"` because the cleaner stands about 70%
// across the frame: a centred crop cuts her off and a right-edge crop pushes
// her to the left of the panel. 86% puts her in the middle of it.
//
// ⚠️ GENERATED, NOT PHOTOGRAPHED, and note the hi-vis exception above.
//
// In `hero`, on `headingLines`:
// Brief §4. The mapped primary `commercial warehouse cleaning services`
// (60/mo) appeared nowhere in the old H1, and the H1 is scored present or
// absent. Region is the extension, because this is the only heading slot on
// the page that can carry it and the page otherwise never says where it
// works above the fold.
//
// The old line — the best single sentence on the page — is not cut. It opens
// the lead, because it works as a flat contradiction of an assumption and
// adding six words to it kills the timing.
// In `hero`, on `subheading`:
// Brief §5. Rule 5's second slot, which this page did not have. Its
// extension is the PRICING STRUCTURE rather than the H1's region, and it
// puts the page's central commercial argument above the fold: the floor and
// the amenities are two different jobs and a good quote prices them
// separately. The body says that three times and never before the scroll.
// In `hero`, on `lead`:
// Brief §6. The region comes out because the new H1 carries it. "Amenities
// done properly" becomes "the crib room and bathrooms done daily", which is
// more specific and matches the section the page argues hardest, and "a
// scope that says which is which" gains "written", which is the word the
// pricing block relies on.

// §2 Definition. Answer-target block. Paragraph two names the split that the
// rest of the page is built on and that most quotes silently get wrong.
//
// In `definitionBody`, on paragraph 1:
// Brief §10. The opening paragraph is worth 10 of the 100 primary-keyword
// points and needs the mapped phrase inside the first two sentences. Four
// words changed does it; the scope list is untouched.

// §3 The boundary. `warning`, and FIRST — before any scope.
//
// On an industrial site the dangerous contractor is the one who says yes to
// everything, so this block is the page refusing four things by name. Same
// structural pattern as the construction page's silica callout, the medical
// page's clinical waste and the kitchen page's canopy certification.
//
// ⚠️ VERIFICATION PASS REQUIRED, and all four refusals below are checkable:
//   - Work at height above two metres attracts specific fall-prevention
//     duties in NSW, and using an elevating work platform requires
//     appropriate training and, above a boom length threshold, a high risk
//     work licence. Correct in substance. NO HEIGHT OR BOOM FIGURE IS QUOTED
//     as a licensing threshold, on purpose — those numbers move and a wrong
//     one here would be actively dangerous.
//   - Forklift operation requires a high risk work licence in NSW. Correct.
//   - Pallet racking inspection is a specialist engineering assessment, not a
//     cleaning observation. Correct.
//   - A spill of unknown substance requires the site's own emergency
//     procedure and the Safety Data Sheet, not a general cleaner with a mop.
//     Correct, and the most important of the four.
//   - Safe Work Australia and SafeWork NSW are the right primary sources, and
//     the brand foundation document (§3.3) already approves them.

// §4 Scope, grouped BY ZONE — floor, racking, dock, amenities, office,
// periodic. That is the grouping a warehouse manager walks the site in, and
// it differs from the office page's frequency grouping, strata's area
// grouping and the kitchen page's difficulty grouping.
//
// ⚠️ EVERY ITEM IS DRAFTED against standard practice, not supplied by TLB.
// The floor item carries the biggest bracket on the page: without a machine,
// this page is not honest.
//
// In `zoneItems`, on "The floor: machine scrubbed, not mopped" (description):
// ⚠️ THE bracket. See the file header.

// §5 The amenities argument. `ContentGrid columns={2}` with an `image` cell —
// THE ONLY USE OF ContentGrid's `image` cell type IN THE CLUSTER, and it is
// here because the argument needs the reader to look at a crib room and a
// dock and notice that one of them is the one their team actually lives in.
//
// This is the asymmetry the file header describes: the floor got six lines in
// §4, and the smallest zone gets its own section.

// §6 "Worth knowing". The lever here is that a warehouse floor and a
// warehouse's dust are both safety items rather than cosmetic ones, which
// reframes the whole spend.
//
// ⚠️ VERIFICATION PASS REQUIRED:
//   - A person conducting a business or undertaking has a primary duty under
//     the model WHS laws to provide and maintain a work environment without
//     risks to health and safety, and housekeeping sits inside that.
//     Correct in substance. NO SECTION NUMBER IS QUOTED, on purpose.
//   - Slips, trips and falls are a leading cause of workplace injury in
//     Australia. Correct in substance; no statistic quoted, because
//     trust.ts already carries a standing warning about unsourced figures on
//     this site.
//   - Accumulated combustible dust is a recognised fire and, in the right
//     conditions, explosion risk in industrial settings. Correct, and
//     deliberately hedged to the settings where it applies.
//   - Sealed concrete deteriorates faster under tyre rubber and abrasive dust
//     if not cleaned; re-sealing is a capital cost. Correct in substance.

// §7 Related pages. Factories is the nearest neighbour and construction the
// second, since a new industrial unit gets a builders clean before it gets a
// contract. Pressure cleaning is appended because the hardstand is half of
// what a visitor sees.
const relatedTags = relatedPremises('/commercial-cleaning/warehouse-and-industrial-cleaning/');

// §9 Branded FAQs, in the CUSTOMER'S voice — a warehouse, operations or site
// manager.
//
// In `brandedFaqItems`, on "Can your team meet our site induction?" (answer):
// ⚠️ Real bracket. An industrial site will not let anyone past the
// gate without this.
// In `brandedFaqItems`, on "Do you do the floor with a machine?" (answer):
// ⚠️ Same bracket as §4. This is the page's honesty test.

// §10 Non-branded FAQs, the long-tail block.
//
// ⚠️ VERIFICATION PASS REQUIRED. Checkable claims:
//   - Autoscrubbers remove soil rather than redistributing it, and are the
//     standard method for large sealed concrete floors. Correct.
//   - Concrete floor sealing and its deterioration under abrasive soil.
//     Correct in substance.
//   - Model WHS duty to provide and maintain a work environment without
//     risks. Correct; no section quoted.
//   - Combustible dust risk applies in specific industries. Correct and
//     hedged.
//   - Forklift operation requires a high risk work licence in NSW. Correct.
//   - No dollar figure anywhere, same as every sibling page.
//
// In `nonBrandedFaqItems`, on "How much does warehouse cleaning cost?" (answer):
// ⚠️ BRACKETED ON PURPOSE, same as every sibling page.

// §11 Closing CTA.
// The closing lead ends on the full approved CTA sentence, which used to be
// a separate constant (`primaryCtaSentence`). It is now part of that lead in
// the content file.

// CONTENT lives in src/content/pages/commercial-cleaning/warehouse-and-industrial-cleaning.yaml
// and is edited in Pages CMS ("Warehouse and industrial cleaning"). This file owns the layout. The
// notes above explain why each section says what it says; they stay here
// because Pages CMS rewrites the YAML on save and would drop them.
const page = await getPage(
  'commercial-cleaning/warehouse-and-industrial-cleaning',
  z.object({
    seo: section.seo,
    // The label of the page's main button. It links to the quote page in Site
    // settings. Empty falls back to the site-wide walkthrough label.
    ctaLabel: section.optional(section.text),
    hero: section.hero,
    // Its background photo sits behind the trust bar and this block together
    // (the Backdrop below), so it cannot be left empty.
    definition: section.textBlock.extend({ backgroundImage: section.backgroundPhoto }),
    boundary: section.callout,
    scope: section.iconGrid,
    amenities: section.contentGrid,
    worthKnowing: section.textBlock,
    // The pills are the other premises pages, from Site settings.
    related: section.tagCloud.omit({ tags: true }).extend({ note: section.optional(z.array(section.text)) }),
    reviews: section.sectionHeading,
    // The subheading falls back to the shared service-area line, and the towns
    // come from Site settings.
    whereWeClean: section.tagCloud.omit({ tags: true }).extend({ subheading: section.optional(section.text) }),
    // Heading only. The paragraphs are the shared brand lines.
    brandLine: section.sectionHeading,
    brandedFaq: section.faq,
    faq: section.faq,
    closingCta: section.callToAction,
  }),
);

const pageMeta = {
  ...page.seo,
  canonical: 'https://tlbcleaning.com.au/commercial-cleaning/warehouse-and-industrial-cleaning/',
};

const walkthroughCta = { label: page.ctaLabel ?? walkthroughCtaLabel, href: quoteCta.href };

const heroImage = page.hero.image && sized(page.hero.image, '16/9');

const amenitiesBlocks = page.amenities.items.map((item) =>
  item.type === 'image' ? { type: 'image' as const, ...sized(item.image, '4/3') } : item,
);

const business = commercialBusiness(pageMeta.description);
---

<Base title={pageMeta.title} description={pageMeta.description} canonical={pageMeta.canonical} business={business}>
  <SiteHeader
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: logoImg }}
    primaryNav={primaryNav}
    serviceNav={headerNav}
    secondaryCta={headerSecondaryCta}
    cta={quoteCta}
  />

  <main id="main">
    <Hero
      variant="split-single-image"
      imagePosition="right"
      imageFocus="86%"
      kicker={page.hero.kicker}
      headingLines={page.hero.headingLines}
      subheading={page.hero.subheading}
      lead={page.hero.lead}
      cta={page.hero.cta ?? walkthroughCta}
      image={heroImage}
    />

    <Backdrop image={page.definition.backgroundImage} tint="muted" opacity={90}>
      <TrustBar variant="card" cards={trustBarCards} />
      <TextBlock
        theme="muted"
        align="left"
        heading={page.definition.heading}
        body={page.definition.body}
        cta={page.definition.cta}
      />
    </Backdrop>

    {/* §3 — the four refusals, before any scope. On an industrial site the
        dangerous contractor is the one who says yes to everything. */}
    <Callout tone="warning" heading={page.boundary.heading} body={page.boundary.body} cta={page.boundary.cta} />

    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="icon-grid"
      heading={page.scope.heading}
      lead={page.scope.lead}
      items={page.scope.items}
      cta={page.scope.cta ?? walkthroughCta}
    />

    {/* §5 — the only use of ContentGrid's `image` cell type in the cluster.
        Array order is the layout, so this reads text / photo / photo / text:
        the crib room argument beside the crib room, then the dock beside the
        dock. The asymmetry with §4 is deliberate — see the file header. */}
    <ContentGrid heading={page.amenities.heading} lead={page.amenities.lead} columns={2} blocks={amenitiesBlocks} />

    <TextBlock
      theme="dark"
      align="left"
      heading={page.worthKnowing.heading}
      body={page.worthKnowing.body}
      cta={page.worthKnowing.cta}
      backgroundImage={page.worthKnowing.backgroundImage}
    />

    {/* ⚠️ RESERVED SLOT: before and after slider (BeforeAfter.astro).

        THE PHOTO BRIEF for this page: one aisle of sealed concrete, shot from
        a locked-off tripod, before and after a machine scrub. Concrete is the
        third-best before/after subject on this cluster after carpet and
        rubber gym flooring, and it is the one that makes the §4 machine
        argument visible rather than assertable. Nothing moved between the two
        frames. Drop it in here, between "Worth knowing" and the related
        pages. */}

    <TagCloud
      heading={page.related.heading}
      subheading={page.related.subheading}
      tags={relatedTags}
      note={page.related.note ?? []}
    />

    <GoogleReviewSlider heading={page.reviews.heading} reviews={googleReviews} profileUrl={googleBusinessProfileUrl} />

    <TagCloud
      heading={page.whereWeClean.heading}
      subheading={page.whereWeClean.subheading ?? locationSubheading}
      groups={locationGroups}
      note={page.whereWeClean.note}
    />

    {/* §1.3 The Line as a section heading, with §1.4 as its standfirst.
        The copy, and the reason this page gets `fast` rather than the other
        variant, both live in data/brand-lines.ts. Change it there, not here.

        `muted`, not `dark`: TagCloud above paints --color-brand and Faq below
        paints --color-surface, so Cream between them keeps the page
        alternating instead of stacking two dark bands.

        No CTA prop. §9.5 wants one primary CTA per page, repeated, and the
        closing CallToAction is directly under the FAQs. */}
    <TextBlock
      theme="muted"
      align="left"
      heading={page.brandLine.heading}
      body={[managedForYou.recurring, ...theLineBody.commercial, ...howItWorks.general]}
    />

    {/* Brief §20. The six questions here are about site induction, shift
        timing, machine use, forklifts, pallet wrap and what happens on
        contact — all pre-booking questions. The carpet, kitchen and pressure
        pages already use this pattern, so this brings the page into line with
        its siblings and keeps the exact primary out of a fourth heading slot.
        The second heading stays: it carries "warehouse cleaning" but has
        neither "commercial" nor "services", so it is not a fourth instance. */}
    <Faq heading={page.brandedFaq.heading} lead={page.brandedFaq.lead} items={page.brandedFaq.items} />
    <Faq heading={page.faq.heading} lead={page.faq.lead} items={page.faq.items} />

    <CallToAction
      variant="secondary"
      kicker={page.closingCta.kicker}
      heading={page.closingCta.heading}
      lead={page.closingCta.lead}
      cta={page.closingCta.cta ?? walkthroughCta}
    />
  </main>

  <SiteFooter
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: footerLogoImg }}
    columns={[
      { title: 'Services', links: footerServiceLinks },
      { title: 'Locations', links: [{ label: 'View all locations', href: '/locations/' }] },
    ]}
    contact={footerContact}
    copyright={footerCopyright}
  />
</Base>
